{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# BNN + CVaR + Chance-Constrained Production Planning\n","\n","This notebook uses one posterior predictive demand distribution and compares three decision rules:\n","\n","1. expected-cost / SAA optimization,\n","2. CVaR95 optimization,\n","3. a 95% empirical service-level chance constraint.\n","\n","The uncertainty model is the same; only the **risk preference** changes.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import random, numpy as np, pandas as pd, torch, torch.nn as nn, pyro\n","import pyro.distributions as dist\n","from pyro.infer import SVI, Trace_ELBO, Predictive\n","from pyro.infer.autoguide import AutoDiagonalNormal\n","from pyro.nn import PyroModule, PyroSample\n","import pyomo.environ as pyo\n","\n","SEED=7\n","random.seed(SEED); np.random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED); pyro.set_rng_seed(SEED)\n","torch.set_default_dtype(torch.float32)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Train a compact demand BNN\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["n=280; day=np.arange(n)\n","promo=np.random.binomial(1,.25,n); weekend=((day%7)>=5).astype(float)\n","temp=22+8*np.sin(2*np.pi*day/90)+np.random.normal(0,2,n)\n","season=np.sin(2*np.pi*day/30); trend=day/(n-1)\n","mu=108+18*promo+9*weekend+12*season+.42*temp+7*trend\n","demand=mu+np.random.normal(0,7.5,n)\n","Xr=np.column_stack([promo,weekend,temp,season,trend]).astype(np.float32); yr=demand.astype(np.float32)\n","Xm,Xs=Xr.mean(0,keepdims=True),Xr.std(0,keepdims=True)+1e-6; ym,ys=float(yr.mean()),float(yr.std()+1e-6)\n","X=torch.tensor((Xr-Xm)/Xs); y=torch.tensor((yr-ym)/ys)\n","\n","class BNN(PyroModule):\n","    def __init__(self,d,h=16):\n","        super().__init__(); self.h=PyroModule[nn.Linear](d,h); self.o=PyroModule[nn.Linear](h,1)\n","        self.h.weight=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.8).expand([h,d]).to_event(2)); self.h.bias=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.8).expand([h]).to_event(1))\n","        self.o.weight=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.8).expand([1,h]).to_event(2)); self.o.bias=PyroSample(dist.Normal(0,.8).expand([1]).to_event(1))\n","    def forward(self,x,y=None):\n","        m=self.o(torch.tanh(self.h(x))).squeeze(-1); s=pyro.sample('sigma',dist.LogNormal(-1,.35)); pyro.deterministic('mu',m)\n","        with pyro.plate('data',x.shape[0]): pyro.sample('obs',dist.Normal(m,s),obs=y)\n","        return m\n","\n","pyro.clear_param_store(); model=BNN(X.shape[1]); guide=AutoDiagonalNormal(model)\n","svi=SVI(model,guide,pyro.optim.Adam({'lr':.01}),loss=Trace_ELBO())\n","for _ in range(2500): svi.step(X,y)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Posterior predictive scenarios\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["future=np.array([[1,1,32,.45,1.03]],dtype=np.float32); xf=torch.tensor((future-Xm)/Xs)\n","out=Predictive(model,guide=guide,num_samples=5000,return_sites=('obs',))(xf)\n","samples=out['obs'].detach().numpy().reshape(-1)*ys+ym\n","rng=np.random.default_rng(SEED); S=600; d=rng.choice(samples,S,replace=False)\n","print('Demand quantiles:',np.quantile(samples,[.05,.5,.95]).round(2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Expected-cost decision\n","\n","Scenario loss is production cost plus holding and shortage cost.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["c,h,p=1.0,.30,5.0\n","def solve_expected(d):\n","    M=pyo.ConcreteModel(); M.S=pyo.RangeSet(0,len(d)-1); M.x=pyo.Var(domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals); M.e=pyo.Var(M.S,domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals); M.u=pyo.Var(M.S,domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals)\n","    M.ec=pyo.Constraint(M.S,rule=lambda m,s:m.e[s]>=m.x-float(d[s])); M.uc=pyo.Constraint(M.S,rule=lambda m,s:m.u[s]>=float(d[s])-m.x)\n","    M.obj=pyo.Objective(expr=c*M.x+(1/len(d))*sum(h*M.e[s]+p*M.u[s] for s in M.S))\n","    pyo.SolverFactory('appsi_highs').solve(M); return pyo.value(M.x)\n","x_mean=solve_expected(d); print('Expected-cost decision:',round(x_mean,2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. CVaR95 decision\n","\n","For scenario loss \(L_s(x)\), Rockafellar–Uryasev gives\n","\n","\\[CVaR_\\alpha(L)=\\min_\\eta\\left[\\eta+\\frac{1}{1-\\alpha}E(L-\\eta)^+\\right].\n","\n","We optimize a weighted production cost plus CVaR of inventory/shortage loss.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["alpha=.95\n","M=pyo.ConcreteModel(); M.S=pyo.RangeSet(0,S-1); M.x=pyo.Var(domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals); M.e=pyo.Var(M.S,domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals); M.u=pyo.Var(M.S,domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals); M.eta=pyo.Var(); M.z=pyo.Var(M.S,domain=pyo.NonNegativeReals)\n","M.ec=pyo.Constraint(M.S,rule=lambda m,s:m.e[s]>=m.x-float(d[s])); M.uc=pyo.Constraint(M.S,rule=lambda m,s:m.u[s]>=float(d[s])-m.x)\n","M.tail=pyo.Constraint(M.S,rule=lambda m,s:m.z[s]>=h*m.e[s]+p*m.u[s]-m.eta)\n","M.obj=pyo.Objective(expr=c*M.x+M.eta+(1/((1-alpha)*S))*sum(M.z[s] for s in M.S))\n","pyo.SolverFactory('appsi_highs').solve(M); x_cvar=pyo.value(M.x); print('CVaR95 decision:',round(x_cvar,2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Empirical 95% service-level decision\n","\n","For a single production quantity, the empirical chance constraint is satisfied by choosing the 95th percentile of demand scenarios. This is an empirical scenario rule, not a formal distribution-free guarantee.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["x_chance=float(np.quantile(d,.95)); print('Empirical 95% chance-constraint decision:',round(x_chance,2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Out-of-sample comparison\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["eval_d=rng.choice(samples,10000,replace=True)\n","def loss(x,D): return c*x+h*np.maximum(x-D,0)+p*np.maximum(D-x,0)\n","rows=[]\n","for name,x in [('Expected cost',x_mean),('CVaR95',x_cvar),('Chance 95%',x_chance)]:\n","    L=loss(x,eval_d); q=np.quantile(L,.95)\n","    rows.append({'method':name,'production':x,'expected_cost':L.mean(),'CVaR95':L[L>=q].mean(),'stockout_probability':np.mean(eval_d>x)})\n","pd.DataFrame(rows).round(3)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Takeaway\n","\n","The same BNN posterior can support very different operational policies. Choosing between expected cost, CVaR, and a service-level constraint is a decision-modeling choice, not a property of the BNN.\n"]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.x"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}